/-!
# Composition of generating functions on manifolds

Let `S(q, a)` on `M₁ × M₂` and `T(a, Q)` on `M₂ × M₃` be real functions. They generate
cotangent relations `T*M₁ ⇝ T*M₂` and `T*M₂ ⇝ T*M₃`, with `p = d_q S`, `-d_a S` at `a`, and
`d_a T`, `P = -d_Q T` (`TauCeti.CotangentBundle.generatingSource`,
`TauCeti.CotangentBundle.generatingTarget`). Composing the two relations means matching the
intermediate cotangent points:

`(a, -d_a S(q, a)) = (a, d_a T(a, Q))`.

This is exactly the statement that `a` is a critical point of `a' ↦ S(q, a') + T(a', Q)`
(`TauCeti.CotangentBundle.generatingTarget_eq_generatingSource_iff`).

When this critical point is nondegenerate at `(q₀, a₀, Q₀)`, the intermediate position can be
eliminated near `(q₀, Q₀)`: when `S` and `T` are `C^(n+2)` at the matched points, there is a
`C^(n+1)` stationary branch `b(q, Q) ∈ M₂` through `a₀`, and the function
`R(q, Q) = S(q, b) + T(b, Q)` on `M₁ × M₃`, which is `C^(n+2)` at `(q₀, Q₀)`, generates the
composite relation. On an open neighbourhood of `(q₀, Q₀)`,

`d_q R(q, Q) = d_q S(q, b)`,  `d_Q R(q, Q) = d_Q T(b, Q)`,

and near `((q₀, Q₀), a₀)` the matching equation holds exactly on the graph of `b`
(`TauCeti.CotangentBundle.exists_generatingComposition`). Nondegeneracy is the intrinsic notion
of `TauCeti.IsManifoldNondegenerateCriticalPoint`, and the regularity hypotheses are pointwise, so
no chart enters the hypotheses.

The proof reads `S` and `T` in the preferred charts at `q₀`, `a₀` and `Q₀` and applies the
normed-space statement `TauCeti.exists_cotangentGeneratingComposition`. The charts change the
covectors by the invertible chart derivatives, which preserves the matching equation and
transports the identities for `d_q R` and `d_Q R`.

When `S` and `T` are generating functions of the first kind, so is `R`: if the mixed Hessians
`d_a (d_q S)` and `d_Q (d_a T)` (`TauCeti.mixedHessian`) are invertible at the matched points, then
the mixed Hessian of `R` is invertible at `(q₀, Q₀)`
(`TauCeti.CotangentBundle.isInvertible_mixedHessian_of_comp`,
`TauCeti.CotangentBundle.exists_generatingComposition_isInvertible_mixedHessian`). In the
preferred charts it is `M_S ∘ L⁻¹ ∘ M_T`, with `L` the negative Hessian of
`a ↦ S(q₀, a) + T(a, Q₀)` at `a₀`, and the proof transports the normed-space statement
`TauCeti.isInvertible_cotangentMixedHessian_of_comp` through these charts. Each of `S`, `T` and
`R` then generates a local canonical transformation of cotangent bundles
(`TauCeti.CotangentBundle.generatedMap`), and near the source point the transformation generated
by `R` is the one generated by `T` after the one generated by `S`
(`TauCeti.CotangentBundle.generatedMap_eventuallyEq_comp`). This is the elimination of the
internal vertex of the open chain `S(q, a) + T(a, Q)`, whose generating relation is the composite
canonical transformation.

All conclusions are local. No assertion is made about critical points of the sum outside the
chosen neighbourhood, nor about a globally defined composite relation. Generated maps are defined
for globally smooth generating functions, so the last statement concerns any smooth function on
`M₁ × M₃` with the relations of `R` near `(q₀, Q₀)`.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.CotangentBundle.exists_generatingComposition`: elimination of the intermediate
  position along a stationary branch.
* `TauCeti.CotangentBundle.isInvertible_mixedHessian_of_comp`,
  `TauCeti.CotangentBundle.exists_generatingComposition_isInvertible_mixedHessian`: the composite
  of generating functions of the first kind is of the first kind.
* `TauCeti.CotangentBundle.generatedMap_eventuallyEq_comp`: the composite generating function
  generates the composite canonical transformation.

## References

* V. I. Arnold, *Mathematical Methods of Classical Mechanics*, second edition,
  Springer, 1989, §48 (composition of canonical transformations).
* A. Weinstein, *Symplectic categories*, Portugaliae Mathematica 67 (2010), 261–278.
* A. Cannas da Silva, *Lectures on Symplectic Geometry*, Lecture Notes in Mathematics 1764,
  Springer, 2001, Section 5 (Proposition 5.2, the generating function of the second iterate).
-/

